{
  "id": "wolfssl-0h3",
  "title": "crypto2dev CryptoCb shim",
  "description": "Implement a wolfSSL CryptoCb provider that routes cryptographic operations through the /dev/crypto2dev kernel interface (from ~/WORK/WOLFKM). This enables wolfSSL to use FIPS-validated kernel crypto without in-process key material. The shim covers all crypto2dev algorithms: AES-CBC/GCM, SHA-2/SHA-3, HMAC, CMAC, HKDF, PBKDF2, RSA, ECDSA, ECDH.",
  "status": "closed",
  "priority": 1,
  "issue_type": "feature",
  "assignee": "Mark Atwood",
  "created_by": "Mark Atwood",
  "created_at": "2026-04-20T19:16:54Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-20T21:11:11Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-04-20T21:11:11Z",
  "notes": "Design decisions: (1) fd pool for OPERATION fds (reuse via RESET, not open-per-op); (2) WOLF_CRYPTO_CB_FREE required for KEY fd and streaming hash cleanup; (3) RSA and ECC sign both receive pre-hashed digest \u2014 maps cleanly to DO_SIGN; (4) FIPS enforcement conditional (REQUIRE_FIPS ioctl only when build flag set); (5) Full algorithm coverage: all crypto2dev ops.",
